[b]Real skirmishers in the skirmisher formation; heavy infantry with a pilum or two stays in the line.[/b]

In the Order of Battle, a formation that prefers [b]Throwing Weapons[/b] takes anyone who carries a throwable. So Legionaries and Menavliatons with one or two pila, and peasants with a stack of stones, end up beside your javelin men. This mod ranks troops by what they actually carry.

[size=5][b]How troops are ranked[/b][/size]
When a formation prefers [b]Throwing Weapons[/b], it fills in this order:
[list]
[*][b]two or more javelin stacks[/b] first
[*]then [b]one stack[/b]
[*]then [b]pila carriers[/b]
[*]and last, peasants with [b]throwing stones[/b]
[/list]
Other formations and preferences work as in the base game.

[size=5][b]Settings[/b][/size]
It works out of the box. With [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/mountandblade2bannerlord/mods/612]Mod Configuration Menu[/url] ([b]optional[/b]) you can turn it on or off and set the minimum throwables a troop needs to count. Without MCM it runs on its defaults: on, minimum 1 throwable.

[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/mountandblade2bannerlord/mods/2006]Harmony[/url] (required)
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/mountandblade2bannerlord/mods/612]Mod Configuration Menu[/url] (optional)
[/list]

[size=5][b]Install[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Vortex:[/b] click Mod Manager Download and enable it.
[*][b]Manual:[/b] extract the zip into [i]Mount & Blade II Bannerlord\Modules\[/i], so you get [i]Modules\BetterSkirmisherSeparation\SubModule.xml[/i]. Enable it in the launcher, below Harmony (and MCM, if you use it).
[/list]

[size=5][b]Good to know[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Game v1.4.8, singleplayer.
[*]Safe to add or remove mid-campaign: it changes no save data.
[*]Also on the [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3811452468]Steam Workshop[/url] and on [url=https://github.com/TraxData313/better-skirmisher-separation/releases/latest]GitHub Releases[/url]. Same files.
[/list]

Bugs or a mod it fights with: tell me in the comments or on [url=https://github.com/TraxData313/better-skirmisher-separation/issues]GitHub[/url]. How it works in detail: [url=https://github.com/TraxData313/better-skirmisher-separation/blob/main/docs/TECHNICAL.md]docs/TECHNICAL.md[/url].

